    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) and **Junior Caminero** (84.24), who both command elite status against favorable matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** faces Bieber in a spot that exploits the opposing pitcher's 5.48 xERA, while **Junior Caminero** benefits from a strong park factor and a generous SP skill advantage against Lorenzen. **Christian Yelich** (74.32) remains a high-floor play, bolstered by a significant platoon edge and a high-leverage opportunity to exploit an opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base potential. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.09) is a key strategic start; despite a slight negative platoon adjustment, his position atop the lineup and his ability to weaponize his speed against a sluggish delivery make him essential to our pursuit of the stolen base category.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly with the lineup for **Pedro Ramirez** (47.93) still pending confirmation. While **Pedro Ramirez** sits in the marginal tier, his inclusion is contingent on the assumed #7 spot, as any drop in the order could push him below our 40-point threshold for game cap preservation. **Trea Turner** (66.07) provides stability despite an elite opposing arm, though his stolen base outlook is tempered by a catcher who controls the running game effectively. As we manage our game caps, we have opted to keep depth pieces like **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Luis Pena** on the bench, as their lack of favorable situational alignments fails to match the output of our primary starters. With **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Chase Meidroth** sidelined by off-days or roster status, our focus is entirely on this core group to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
